  "visual_observations": [
    "The five release renders use one title position, one subtitle rhythm, one inherited frame and one decision-band treatment.",
    "Seventeen canonical Remix SVG icons appear in four functional peer groups. Each group uses the line variant, black treatment and comparable optical weight.",
    "The page compositions vary with the argument while recurring roles remain visually stable.",
    "The capacity chart retains the target vertical-column orientation. The final roadmap gate remains clear of the dependency divider in the actual deck render."
  ],
  "resolved_findings": [
    "The profile and session now keep the selected icon library enabled.",
    "Each page records asset obligations, candidates, selection reasoning and canonical reconstruction bindings.",
    "Generated icon stand-ins were visually reviewed and the final PowerPoint restores the source SVG files."
  ],
  "intentional_variations": [
    "The opening has larger display KPIs and numbered arguments. The opportunity comparison has native chart values. Those data roles differ from the stable title/body/table system.",
    "The responsibility flow, roadmap and financial model have different interior grids and densities. They retain the recurring introduction and decision frame.",
    "Normal-width native fonts produce different glyph shapes and line breaks from image-generated lettering. Generated orange values and callout labels were calibrated to shared roles, with those differences retained in page review records.",
    "The standalone operating-model preview uses144DPI and the other standalone pages160DPI. Their pixel dimensions differ proportionally. The final assembled preview should use one common DPI. Standalone page-number fields all show1 by design."
  ]
